messages:
jen: Quick FYIfound a docs/runtime mismatch for /v1/generate-stream. Docs show JSON-per-chunk; server emits SSE (text/event-stream). Users hitting JSON.parse errors.

tim: Thanks. Where's the snippet?

jen: docs/snippets/node/generate-stream.md and docs/snippets/python/generate_stream.py. Customer error: SyntaxError: Unexpected token d in JSON at position 0.

alyssa: Proposed quick Node fix:
```js
stream.on('data', chunk => {
  const text = chunk.toString()
  text.split(/\r?\n/).forEach(line => {
    if (!line.startsWith('data:')) return
    const payload = JSON.parse(line.replace(/^data:\s*/, ''))
    // handle payload
  })
})
```
Add a line: "Streaming uses SSE framing; parse 'data:' lines or use the SDK streaming helper."

tim: I'll update OpenAPI later today to use text/event-stream for the response media-type. For now land snippet + short migration note so customers have a workaround.

docs-bot: PR created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/511 by tim 1 files changed: node + python snippets, migration-note.md. CI: docs-lint passed.

jen: Customer confirmed the workaround works. We'll follow up with a full migration guide and test vectors.

alyssa: I'll draft the migration guide under docs/migration/streaming-to-sse.md and include curl examples and SDK helper links. ETA EOD.

docs-bot: PR merged: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/511 1 files merged to main. Staging docs updated."
